Q1  HOW MANY MAYBEs CLEAR TO YES 
------------------------------------------------------------------------------ 
Stratum A only: 68 cases drawn simple-random from the MAYBEs with no 
prior adjudication. The calibration cases are excluded -- they were 
selected by earlier audits, so including them would bias this rate. 

Deep-arm verdict distribution on those 68: 

AMBIGUOUS     MATCH      NONE 
        3        47        18 

clearance to YES, at three thresholds 
  any MATCH                        : 47/68 = 69.1% (95% CI 57.4-78.8) 
  MATCH at medium+ confidence      : 47/68 = 69.1% (95% CI 57.4-78.8) 
  + externally CONFIRMED by search : 46/68 = 67.6% (95% CI 55.8-77.6) 

tie-adjusted clearance (post-stratified on the tier's 59.1% / 40.9% tie split; 
this draw of stratum A is 75.0% ties, so the raw rates above run low) 
  any MATCH      : 70.7% (95% CI 59.4-81.9)   raw 69.1%, shift +1.6 pt 
  medium+ conf   : 70.7% (95% CI 59.4-81.9)   raw 69.1%, shift +1.6 pt 
  + confirmed    : 69.5% (95% CI 58.2-80.8)   raw 67.6%, shift +1.9 pt 
  by tie class, any MATCH: 
    tie=TRUE  n=51  34/51 = 66.7% (95% CI 53.0-78.0) 
    tie=FALSE n=17  13/17 = 76.5% (95% CI 52.7-90.4) 

projected onto the 1,044-case augmented MAYBE tier 
  any MATCH      :  738 cases  (95% CI 620-855)  [tie-adj] 
  medium+ conf   :  738 cases  (95% CI 620-855)  [tie-adj] 
  + confirmed    :  726 cases  (95% CI 608-844)  [tie-adj] 

what that does to the benchmark's clear rate (4,748 identities, 2,979 YES) 
  any MATCH      : 62.74% -> 78.28%  (+15.54 points, CI +13.07 to +18.01)  [tie-adj] 
  medium+ conf   : 62.74% -> 78.28%  (+15.54 points, CI +13.07 to +18.01)  [tie-adj] 
  + confirmed    : 62.74% -> 78.03%  (+15.29 points, CI +12.80 to +17.77)  [tie-adj] 

NOT a precision claim. These are a model's verdicts, carrying the error 
rate measured in section (a) above. The ceiling is 69.1% -- a MAYBE whose 
recipient is simply not in the BMF cannot be cleared by any reviewer. 

